 Consider a random variable 
\begin_inset Formula $z$
\end_inset

 with distribution 
\begin_inset Formula $F$
\end_inset

 that has support on 
\begin_inset Formula $[0,+\infty)$
\end_inset

.
 We interpret the random variable as a multiplicative lottery that will
 realize a multiplicative gain for the agent.
 For instance if 
\begin_inset Formula $z$
\end_inset

 turns out to be 2, then the agent's wealth is multiplied by 2.
 Then, the final distribution of wealth of the agent is the random variable
 
\begin_inset Formula $wz$
\end_inset

 where 
\begin_inset Formula $z$
\end_inset

 is distributed 
\begin_inset Formula $F$
\end_inset

.
 We denoted the distribution of this random variable 
\begin_inset Formula $wF$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
