\begin_layout Proof
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

Suppose the agent is risk averse and exhibits non-increasing absolute risk
 aversion.
 By Theorem 25, for each 
\begin_inset Formula $w_{2}>w_{1}$
\end_inset

, there is an increasing and concave function 
\begin_inset Formula $\psi$
\end_inset

 such that 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ t\in\mathbb{R}:u(w_{1}+t)=\psi\left[u(w_{2}+t)\right]$
\end_inset

.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $w-\underline{p}<w$
\end_inset

, then
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{eqnarray*}
u(w-\underline{p}+t) & = & \psi\left[u(w+t)\right]\\
E\left\{ u(w-\underline{p}+l)\right\}  & = & E\left\{ \psi\left[u(w+l)\right]\right\} 
\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset

Since 
\begin_inset Formula $ $
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $E\left\{ u(w-\underline{p}+l)\right\} =u(w)$
\end_inset

, then
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
u(w)=E\left\{ \psi\left[u(w+l)\right]\right\} 
\]

\end_inset

Since 
\begin_inset Formula $\psi$
\end_inset

 is a concave function, then 
\begin_inset Formula $E\left\{ \psi(u(w+l))\right\} \leq\psi\left[E\left\{ u(w+l)\right\} \right]$
\end_inset

.
 Hence,
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
u(w)\leq\psi\left[E\left\{ u(w+l)\right\} \right]
\]

\end_inset

Since 
\begin_inset Formula $E\left\{ u(w+l)\right\} =u(w+\overline{p})$
\end_inset

, then
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
u(w)\leq\psi\left[u(w+\overline{p})\right]
\]

\end_inset

Since 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ t\in\mathbb{R}:u(w-\underline{p}+t)=\psi\left[u(w+t)\right]$
\end_inset

, then
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
u(w)\leq u(w-\underline{p}+\overline{p})
\]

\end_inset

Since 
\begin_inset Formula $u$
\end_inset

 is monotone, then
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{eqnarray*}
w & \leq & w-\underline{p}+\overline{p}\\
\underline{p} & \leq & \overline{p}
\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset


\bar under
Part D.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Proof
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

Now, suppose that the agent is risk averse and exhibits non-increasing relative
