\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Mean preserving spread
\end_layout

\begin_layout Definition*

\series bold
(126).

\series default
 
\emph on
Let 
\begin_inset Formula $\{F,G\}\subseteq\Delta(\mathbb{R})$
\end_inset

.
 Then, 
\begin_inset Formula $G$
\end_inset

 is a mean preserving spread of 
\begin_inset Formula $F$
\end_inset

 if there is a family of distributions 
\begin_inset Formula $\left\{ H_{x}:x\in\mathbb{R},\ \mu_{H_{x}}=0\right\} $
\end_inset

 such that for each 
\begin_inset Formula $y\in\mathbb{R}$
\end_inset

,
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
G(y)={\displaystyle \int_{-\infty}^{\infty}}\left({\displaystyle \int_{-\infty}^{y}}dH_{x}(t)\right)dF(x)
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

